# Valve's arm64 steamcmd, for the OpenGamepadUI Steam plugin.
#
# Read by ~/.steam/steamcmd/steamcmd.sh while that is still RetroForge's stub
# (/usr/lib/retroforge/steamcmd-stub, which /usr/lib/retroforge/install-steamcmd puts there before the
# shell starts). The first time the plugin runs steamcmd, the stub downloads this, checks the sha256,
# unpacks it over itself and runs it. From then on ~/.steam/steamcmd is Valve's own steamcmd, which
# updates itself from Valve's manifest (media.steampowered.com/client/steam_cmd_linuxarm64).
#
# WHY. The plugin (ShadowBlip/OpenGamepadUI-steam, core/steam_client.gd) runs
# ~/.steam/steamcmd/steamcmd.sh for the library, installs and updates. When that file is missing it
# downloads Valve's x86 bootstrapper (steamcmd_linux.tar.gz: an i386 binary), which cannot run here.
# It downloads only when steamcmd.sh is missing, so the stub sitting there stops it.
#
# Not in the image: everything that can be downloaded is. It is 4 MB the plugin only needs once a
# player opens Steam, and the player's copy replaces itself with Valve's updates anyway.
#
# WHAT IS IN IT (checked 2026-10-15): steamcmd.sh + linuxarm64/{steamcmd, crashhandler.so,
# steamerrorreporter}, all ELF64 aarch64, NEEDED only glibc (libc/libdl/libm/libpthread, GLIBC_2.30),
# so no Steam Runtime. Valve's steamcmd.sh picks linuxarm64 on `uname -m` = aarch64 and linux32
# otherwise. The stub refuses a tarball without steamcmd.sh and linuxarm64/steamcmd.
#
# ARMv8.0 (SM6115): NOT LSE-clean. steamcmd has ~300 unguarded LSE atomics (281 ldaddal, casal,
# swpa, ...), crashhandler.so ~135, steamerrorreporter 5, with no outline-atomic helpers, which is the
# same toolchain as Valve's arm64 client (docs/steam-arm64.md). The SM8250/SM8550/SM8650 boards run it
# natively. The Air X needs kernel/patches/0025 (LSE emulation) or it SIGILLs as soon as steamcmd goes
# multithreaded. It is Valve's binary, so this cannot be fixed with a rebuild.
#
# Same fields as runtime.pin and a packages/*/prebuilt.pin (the stub reads name/version/url/sha256).
#
# TO BUMP. The URL is unversioned and Valve replaces it in place, so a "sha256 mismatch" from the stub
# means Valve republished the bootstrapper, not a corrupt download. Until this is bumped and the
# update ships, a player who has not run steamcmd yet gets that error and no steamcmd; players who
# have are not affected (their copy is Valve's, self-updating, and install-steamcmd never replaces a
# working arm64 copy). Re-check the layout, the ELF arch and the LSE count of the new one, then set
# version (its Last-Modified date) + sha256 together.
name: steamcmd
version: 20260727
url: https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/client/installer/steamcmd_linuxarm64.tar.gz
sha256: 32eef1a7c3fd98bed9e1bd0bf6bdc41a3c7c58583351a1d802f449e623f7a86c
